    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you. but honestly, isn't there a point where these \"valid concerns\" just become excuses to prevent much-needed housing supply? it feels like every time a new project comes up, people use \"neighborhood character\" as a way to essentially block anything that isn't a single-family home, which just makes the housing crisis worse. doesn't that make their position kind of indefensible in the long run?",
